{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n038d must remove eight live env/config aliases and move all runtime/test consumers to canonical spellings. ADR 0116 is the governing decision for this leaf: it authorizes clean pre-1.0 removal for simplification with no expected clients, and explicitly says the follow-on implementation must not keep the aliases as permanent aliases or convert them into fail-loud tombstones merely because they once existed.\n\nThe previous plan language used \"tombstone\" / \"removed-input\" wording. This plan reconciles that conflict toward ADR 0116 and the 038d operator approval: delete the alias declarations and active parsing/warning paths outright. The old spellings should be absent from active config behavior; canonical spellings remain supported and preserve their prior typed behavior and precedence. Published config docs and release notes are deliberately sequenced to dependent ticket `1a63-056e-98b9-4ab7`; this leaf only regenerates doc surfaces that are mechanically coupled to the live config/deprecation registries so CI drift checks pass after the code removal.\n\n## Approach\n\nDelete the eight `_permanent(...)` rows for these retired spellings from `src/rebar/_deprecations.py`:\n\n| Removed alias | Canonical replacement |\n| --- | --- |\n| `REBAR_NO_SYNC` | `REBAR_SYNC_PULL=off` |\n| `COMPACT_THRESHOLD` | `REBAR_COMPACT_THRESHOLD` |\n| `SCRATCH_BASE_DIR` | `REBAR_SCRATCH_BASE_DIR` |\n| `REBAR_ACLI_TIMEOUT` | `REBAR_JIRA_CLI_TIMEOUT` |\n| `RECONCILER_ABSENT_GET_BUDGET` | `REBAR_RECONCILER_DELETION_PROBE_LIMIT` |\n| `REBAR_ID_GUARD_MODE=warn` | `REBAR_UNSAFE_ID_GUARD_BYPASS=true` |\n| `REBAR_VERIFY_OVERLAP_ENABLED` | `REBAR_VERIFY_SUGGEST_DUPLICATE_TICKETS` |\n| `verify.overlap_enabled` | `verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets` |\n\nRemove the corresponding active environment parsing, inversion/transformation, mapping, and deprecation-warning paths from `src/rebar/_config_sources.py`. Remove `verify.overlap_enabled` from `src/rebar/_config_sections._ALIASES` and update `src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py` so the config display no longer rewrites the retired TOML key. Update source-level guidance that still presents these names as live aliases, including `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py`, `src/rebar/_reads.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/rebar_id_audit.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/compact.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/scratch.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_init.py`, and `src/rebar/llm/build_drift.py`.\n\nRegenerate `docs/env-vars.md` and `docs/config-reference.md` from the registries. Update `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py` and `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py` so the doc-drift gates expect the retired env/config spellings to be absent, matching the existing removed-var checks. Migrate dedicated alias-behavior tests from warn+map expectations to clean-removal assertions: each retired spelling is ignored as an unknown environment/config input, produces no legacy alias deprecation warning, and does not override the canonical/default value. Migrate functional consumer tests to canonical spellings only.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_deprecations.py`, `src/rebar/_config_sources.py`, `src/rebar/_config_sections.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py`\n- source guidance / runtime consumers: `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py`, `src/rebar/_reads.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/rebar_id_audit.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/compact.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/scratch.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_init.py`, `src/rebar/llm/build_drift.py`\n- generated registry/doc-drift coverage: `docs/env-vars.md`, `docs/config-reference.md`, `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py`, `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py`\n- alias-behavior suites: `tests/unit/test_config_sync_aliases.py`, `tests/unit/test_config_ev3a_aliases.py`, `tests/unit/test_config_alias_overlap_rename.py`, `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_ev3c_env_renames.py`, `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_config_file_wiring.py`\n- functional consumers migrated to canonical names: `tests/integration/test_store_concurrency.py`, `tests/interfaces/queries/test_next_batch_compute.py`, `tests/interfaces/store/test_bridge_preview_under_sync_contention_heldout.py`, `tests/unit/test_read_freshness_parity.py`, `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/conflict/test_conflict_resolver_no_rebar_id_writes.py`, `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_rebar_id_label_writers.py`, `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_differ_bound_but_absent.py`, `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_outbound_differ_bound_but_absent.py`, and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_get_rotation_heldout.py`\n\n## Explicit non-goals / sequencing\n\n- Do not add fail-loud tombstones or `_tomb(...)` rows for these aliases.\n- Do not perform the publication pass for authored config docs, examples, changelog, or release notes in this leaf; that is dependent ticket `1a63-056e-98b9-4ab7`, which depends on this code-removal leaf so it can publish after the canonical behavior lands.\n\n## Testing\n\nRED-first oracle coverage will assert every retired spelling is no longer an active alias parser/mapper and no longer emits the legacy deprecation warning. For environment aliases, setting only the old variable must leave the canonical setting at its default; setting both old and canonical variables must use the canonical variable exactly as before. For the retired TOML key, `verify.overlap_enabled` must no longer populate `verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets` or appear as an alias display row.\n\nCanonical parity tests must prove the prior typed behavior and precedence for `REBAR_SYNC_PULL=off`, `REBAR_COMPACT_THRESHOLD`, `REBAR_SCRATCH_BASE_DIR`, `REBAR_JIRA_CLI_TIMEOUT`, `REBAR_RECONCILER_DELETION_PROBE_LIMIT`, `REBAR_UNSAFE_ID_GUARD_BYPASS=true`, `REBAR_VERIFY_SUGGEST_DUPLICATE_TICKETS`, `verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets`, and the read-freshness opt-out path. A residual-reference sweep over source, tests, and generated registry docs for all eight old spellings must be machine-checkable; remaining references must be confined to ADR/history/release-note material, dependent publication-ticket material, and the negative assertions in this leaf's tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The eight removed spellings have no active alias parser/mapper/warning and are absent from the live deprecation alias registry.\n- [ ] `verify.overlap_enabled` is removed from live alias enrollment and the config-surface render path no longer rewrites or displays it as an alias.\n- [ ] Dedicated alias-behavior suites assert clean removal rather than warn+map or fail-loud tombstone behavior.\n- [ ] All functional consumers of the eight removed spellings use canonical inputs instead, including read-freshness and deletion-probe-budget paths.\n- [ ] Generated registry docs (`docs/env-vars.md`, `docs/config-reference.md`) and their drift tests reflect the removal; broader publication docs/changelog/release-note updates remain sequenced to dependent ticket `1a63-056e-98b9-4ab7`.\n- [ ] Canonical config/env spellings still preserve the prior typed behavior and precedence rules they replace, including sync pull, compact threshold, scratch base dir, Jira CLI timeout, deletion probe limit, unsafe-ID-guard bypass, duplicate-ticket suggestion, and read-freshness opt-out."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788552417409773650,"uuid":"615eb921-86a4-485d-82a0-03692b495cdb"}